* text=auto eol=lf

# Recorded traffic archives and rendering baselines are binary and must never
# be line-ending-normalised — the compat and snapshot gates compare bytes.
tests/compat/**/*.har   binary
tests/compat/**/*.warc  binary
tests/**/*.png          binary
data/**                 binary

# The HTML conformance corpus is byte-exact test data, not text. Several files
# deliberately contain carriage returns, because how the tokenizer treats CR is
# one of the things they test.
#
# Today those are lone CRs, which `text=auto eol=lf` happens to leave alone --
# checked against upstream, byte-identical. That is luck rather than design: a
# future corpus update carrying a meaningful CRLF would be normalised to LF on
# commit, and the test would then be asserting something the corpus does not
# say. Marked binary so the question stops arising.
tests/html5lib/**/*.dat binary

# Committed fonts are binary.
tests/fonts/**/*.ttf binary
tests/fonts/**/*.otf binary

# The vendored test262 subset is byte-exact. Several tests deliberately contain
# CR, LS and PS characters, which line-ending normalisation would change.
tests/test262/** binary
